// Package achievements declares a game's achievements once, in a versioned YAML file, tracks each player's progress toward them, and reports that progress through NSGo's platform game services: Game Center on macOS, iOS and tvOS, and Google Play Games Services on Android.
//
// # Definitions
//
// A Set is the parsed form of an achievements file such as achievements.yaml. Each Definition has a game-wide ID that game code uses, an optional title and description for the game's own UI, a step count (1 for a one-shot achievement, more for one that fills up, such as "clear 500 gems"), and the ID each platform service knows it by. Game Center IDs are chosen by the developer in App Store Connect, Play Games IDs are generated by Play Console, so each service's ID is written out explicitly; an achievement without an ID for a service is not reported to that service.
//
// Parse refuses unknown fields, unsupported versions, duplicate IDs and malformed platform IDs. Encode writes deterministic 2-space YAML, and a file Encode wrote parses and encodes back to the same bytes.
//
// # Progress
//
// A Tracker holds the steps the player has made toward each achievement. Progress only moves forward: SetSteps ignores a lower count, Add saturates at the achievement's step count, and Unlock completes it. OnUnlock is called once when an achievement completes.
//
// The Tracker remembers, per service, the steps the service last acknowledged, so progress made offline or before sign-in is reported once a service is connected, and progress a service already has is not sent again. Progress and EncodeProgress give that state as a versioned YAML document; Persist keeps it in core.Storage (or any Store) and rewrites it after every change.
//
// # Game services
//
// SignIn picks the service for the running platform with ServiceFor, signs the player in with gameservices.Authenticate and, once signed in, connects the Tracker to a Reporter backed by gameservices.ReportAchievement, which reports everything pending. Where the platform has no game service (Windows, Linux, the web, watchOS) SignIn answers gameservices.ErrUnsupported and the Tracker keeps counting locally. Call gameservices.ShowAchievements to open the platform's own achievements screen.
package achievements
